-- title:
--   Integrality of the C-fibre of a Čerednik–Drinfeld quotient
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$ and a characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ that is a discrete valuation ring, with an irreducible element $\pi$ such that $\mathcal O$ is $(\pi)$-adically complete, $\#(\mathcal O/(\pi))=r$ and $(r)=(\pi)$, and let $K_0$ be a characteristic-zero field that is the fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Let $Onr$ be a characteristic-zero domain over $\mathcal O$ with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that ideal being maximal, every element of $Onr$ satisfying a monic $\mathcal O$-polynomial modulo it, every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree having a root modulo it, and $\mathrm{Fr}(x)\equiv x^{r}$ modulo it. Let $v\!\det:\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) satisfy $v\!\det(g)=n$ exactly when $\det g=u\pi^{n}$ for a unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$. Let $G$ be a group, $\sigma:G\to\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ a homomorphism, $\Gamma\le G$ a subgroup containing an element whose image is scalar with $v\!\det=2$ and an element with $v\!\det=1$, and $\Gamma'$ the subgroup whose elements are exactly those of $\Gamma$ with even $v\!\det\circ\sigma$; let $\rho:G\to\mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ be the projectivisation of $\sigma$, and assume the image of $\Gamma'$ acts on the vertices of the lattice tree of $\mathcal O$ in $K_0$ with finite stabilisers and with finitely many orbits. Let $f:\mathcal X\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ be proper and flat, and assume its base change along $\operatorname{Spec}K_0\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ (the second pullback projection) is smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically connected. A further block of hypotheses, summarised here, provides a family of maps $\Theta$ sending, for each $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, a pair consisting of an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $Onr\to B$ and a Deligne datum over $B$ to a $B$-point of $f$ (a morphism $\operatorname{Spec}B\to\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$), and requires $\Theta$ to be natural in $B$, invariant under the twisted $\Gamma$-action `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` (Frobenius twist by $-v\!\det$ on the $Onr$-component together with pullback of the Deligne datum along $g^{-1}$), surjective with fibres exactly the twisted $\Gamma$-orbits over each algebraically closed field in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, and initial among such natural invariant families. A final block fixes the analytic data: an algebraically closed, complete valued field $C$ over $K_0$ whose valuation satisfies a rank-one comparison condition and cuts out exactly $\mathcal O$ inside $K_0$, a pseudo-uniformizer $\varpi$ whose underlying element is the image of $\pi$, exhausting the upper half-plane and with $\operatorname{HolRingOf}\varpi\rho$ a domain, a ring map $\psi_0:Onr\to C$ of valuation at most $1$ extending $\mathcal O\to K_0\to C$, and $s_C:\operatorname{Spec}C\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ induced by the composite $\mathcal O\to K_0\to C$. The conclusion is that the fibre product $\mathcal X\times_{\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O}\operatorname{Spec}C$ is an integral scheme.
--
--   This is the integrality statement for the base change to the complete algebraically closed field $C$ of a scheme arising as a Čerednik–Drinfeld quotient, in the variant where smoothness of relative dimension $1$ and geometric connectedness of the generic fibre over $K_0$ are assumed as explicit hypotheses; the conclusion is obtained from [`AlgebraicGeometry.isIntegral_pullback_of_geometricallyConnected_of_smooth_pullback_snd`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.isIntegral_pullback_of_geometricallyConnected_of_smooth_pullback_snd). It is used in the construction of an isomorphism between the function field of the $C$-fibre and the invariant field attached to the level structure.
